paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite50†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL158: \nL159: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite51†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL160: cite52†About†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite55†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite56†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite57†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite58†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite59†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L161: \nL162: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.00807v1] FREESH: Fair, Resource- and Energy-Efficient Scheduling for LLM Serving on Heterogeneous GPUs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.00807v1)\nciteturn2281view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.00807v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 2 Nov 2025 (this version), latest version 5 Nov 2025 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:FREESH: Fair, Resource- and Energy-Efficient Scheduling for LLM Serving on Heterogeneous GPUs\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Xuan He , cite7†Zequan Fang , cite8†Jinzhao Lian , cite9†Danny H.K. Tsang , cite10†Baosen Zhang , cite11†Yize Chen L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled FREESH: Fair, Resource- and Energy-Efficient Scheduling for LLM Serving on Heterogeneous GPUs, by Xuan He and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite12†View PDF cite13†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:The ever-increasing computation and energy demand for LLM and AI agents call for holistic and efficient optimization of LLM serving systems. In practice, heterogeneous GPU clusters can be deployed in a geographically distributed manner, while LLM load also observes diversity in terms of both query traffic and serving patterns.\nL17: LLM queries running on advanced GPUs during a high-emission hour at one location can lead to significantly higher carbon footprints versus same queries running on mid-level GPUs at a low-emission time and location. By observing LLM serving requirements and leveraging spatiotemporal computation flexibility, we consider the joint routing and scheduling problem, and propose FREESH to cooperatively run a group of data centers while minimizing user-specified carbon or energy objectives.\nL18: FREESH identifies the optimal configurations of balanced load serving by matching distinct GPU instance's power-throughput characteristics with predictable LLM query length and workloads. To ensure both latency and fairness requirements, FREESH identifies optimized parallelism and query routing schedules together with dynamic GPU frequency scaling for power saving, and Least-Laxity-First (LLF) serving strategy for query scheduling.\nL19: During the 1-hour serving on production workloads, FREESH reduces energy by 28.6% and emissions by 45.45% together with improvements in SLO attainment and fairness.\nL20: Comments:  | In Submission, code available at cite14†this https URL†github.com L21: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite15†arXiv:2511.00807 [cs.DC]\nL23:    | (or cite16†arXiv:2511.00807v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL24:    | cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.00807†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Yize Chen [cite18†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Sun, 2 Nov 2025 05:17:02 UTC (24,716 KB)\nL29: cite5†[v2] Wed, 5 Nov 2025 18:15:57 UTC (24,129 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Pape